# The CRLF/NUL guard (the world repo's 304890d2 lesson, office copy — Keemin yes 2026-08-23):
# a stray CR or NUL in a source file must not flip git into binary-sniffing a
# .mjs/.md diff into a Bin sweep. Text, LF, always.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
# POS-60: .sh and .yml join the guard for a second reason on top of that one —
# these two run on Linux. A shell script committed with CRLF from a Windows
# checkout fails on the box with `bash: \r: command not found`, and the deploy
# script here IS the deploy. Text, LF, always.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Systemd units run on the box. A CRLF in ExecStart fails as a missing file.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
